window.QAD = {"baseUrl":"https://question-a-day.example/","evergreenFirstStart":"2026-11-17","evergreenLastStart":"2027-06-30","dtstamp":"20261116T120000Z","uidPrefix":"puretome-question-a-day","alarmTrigger":"PT9H","feeds":[{"id":"mom-or-dad","name":"30 days with Mom or Dad","calendarName":"A Question a Day: Mom or Dad","kind":"evergreen","blurb":"Thirty questions for a parent or grandparent, from the first house they remember to the story they most want kept. Starts the day after you add it.","note":"","credit":"","days":[{"q":"What is the first house or apartment you remember living in? Walk me through the front door.","follow":"Which room did you spend the most time in, and why that one?","tip":"Start with a place. Places are easier to describe than feelings, and the people show up on their own."},{"q":"Who lived on your street when you were small? Pick one neighbor you can still picture.","follow":"What did that person do that you noticed as a kid?","tip":"If they name someone you have never heard of, write the name down. It is a thread for another day."},{"q":"What did a school day look like for you at about ten years old, from the time you got up?","follow":"How did you get to school, and who went with you?","tip":"Ask for the ordinary day, not the big one. The ordinary day is the one nobody wrote down."},{"q":"Which teacher or grown-up outside the family do you still think about? Tell me about one day with them.","follow":"What is one thing they said that stuck with you?","tip":"Let them take their time. A pause usually means they are finding the picture."},{"q":"What was an ordinary weeknight supper where you grew up, and who made it?","follow":"Which dish from back then could you still make, or still taste?","tip":"Food questions work at a busy table. Everyone has an opinion, and the answers are funny more often than sad."},{"q":"What was your first paying job? Take me to the first day.","follow":"What did you do with the first money you earned?","tip":"Ask what the work smelled and sounded like. The senses bring back the details."},{"q":"Find a photograph of yourself from when you were young. What was happening just outside the frame?","follow":"Who took it, and what happened right after?","tip":"A person who cannot start a story can almost always explain a photo. Let the picture do some of the asking."},{"q":"Who was your closest friend when you were a teenager? Tell me about one afternoon you spent together.","follow":"Where did the two of you go when you wanted to get away from everyone?","tip":"If the friend has died, give it a moment before the next question. Then ask what they were like."},{"q":"What song takes you straight back to a particular day when you were young? Where were you?","follow":"Who were you with when you heard it?","tip":"If you can, play the song for them. Then be quiet and let it work."},{"q":"What was the first place you lived on your own, or away from the people who raised you?","follow":"What did it cost, and what did you put in it?","tip":"Money details are gold for a story. Ask for prices, not just places."},{"q":"Tell me about a trip you still think about. Where did you go, and who was with you?","follow":"What went wrong on that trip?","tip":"Asking what went wrong usually gets a better story than asking what was best."},{"q":"What is a skill someone taught you by hand? Who taught you, and where were you?","follow":"What did they do differently from how people do it now?","tip":"If it is something they can show you, ask them to show you. Hands remember."},{"q":"Tell me about a holiday from when you were young that you remember clearly, good or not. Where was it?","follow":"Who was there, and who sat where?","tip":"Some holidays were hard. If the answer turns heavy, follow it gently or move on. Both are fine."},{"q":"Where were you when you heard a piece of big news, the kind everyone remembers?","follow":"Who was the first person you talked to about it?","tip":"News days are easy to place in time, which helps you put the rest of the story in order later."},{"q":"What is a job or a role you were proud of, paid or not? Tell me about one day of it.","follow":"Who did you work alongside, and what were they like?","tip":"Halfway. Read back one answer from the first two weeks and ask if you got it right. The corrections are often the best part."},{"q":"What is the hardest physical work you have ever done? Where were you?","follow":"How did you feel at the end of that day?","tip":"When a line lands, write down their exact words. Your summary will never be as good as how they said it."},{"q":"Tell me about a time you got lost, stuck or stranded somewhere. How did you get home?","follow":"Who helped, or who should have?","tip":"Small emergencies make good stories, and they are usually safe to tell at the table."},{"q":"Who made you laugh the most when you were growing up? Tell me about one time.","follow":"What would they say if they walked in right now?","tip":"Ask for an impression. People will often do a voice they have not done in years."},{"q":"What drive, bus ride or train route do you remember best? Where did it take you?","follow":"What did you see out the window?","tip":"A trip gives a story a beginning, a middle and an end without anyone trying."},{"q":"Tell me about a decision that changed where your life went. Where were you when you made it?","follow":"Who did you tell first?","tip":"Do not ask whether it was the right call. Ask what it was like to make it."},{"q":"Where did you go to be alone, or to think, when you were younger? Describe it.","follow":"What did you think about there?","tip":"If they say nowhere, ask where they went when the house got loud."},{"q":"Tell me about someone you lost touch with that you still wonder about.","follow":"Where did you last see them?","tip":"Write down every name you hear today. A list of names is worth a second conversation."},{"q":"What did a Saturday look like for you in your twenties or thirties? Pick one you remember.","follow":"Where did the money go back then, and where did the time go?","tip":"Decades are easier to walk through than single years. Let them pick the decade."},{"q":"What is something you made, built, grew or fixed that you are proud of? Tell me about making it.","follow":"Where is it now?","tip":"Pride is an easier door than regret. Go in through it first."},{"q":"Tell me about a meal you will never forget. Where were you, and who was at the table?","follow":"What was said at that table that you still remember?","tip":"At a family meal, ask while the plates are mostly empty and nobody has stood up yet."},{"q":"Of the people who raised you, who do you think about most? Tell me about one ordinary day with them.","follow":"What do you wish you had asked them?","tip":"This question often turns the conversation around. Let it."},{"q":"What is a piece of advice you ignored? Where were you when you heard it?","follow":"What happened instead?","tip":"Laughter is allowed. Most of these answers are funnier than you expect."},{"q":"Tell me about a year that was hard, and one small thing that got you through it.","follow":"Who showed up for you that year?","tip":"Only if they want to. \"I don't want to get into that\" is a full answer. Say \"that's fine\" and ask about the small thing instead."},{"q":"If you could go back to one place from your life tomorrow, where would it be? What would you do first when you got there?","follow":"Who would you want with you?","tip":"If a small version of this trip is possible, even a drive past an old address, write that down too."},{"q":"What is one moment from your life you would want people to know about a hundred years from now? Tell it the way you want it told.","follow":"Why that one?","tip":"Write this answer down word for word and read it back to them. Then thank them for the thirty days."}]},{"id":"holidays","name":"30 days before the holidays","calendarName":"A Question a Day: the holidays","kind":"fixed","start":"2026-11-26","blurb":"Thirty questions about holidays, food, winters and the people at the table, one a day from Thanksgiving to December 25.","note":"","credit":"","days":[{"q":"What is a Thanksgiving, or any big family meal, from years ago that you can still picture? Where was it?","follow":"Who was at the table, and who did the cooking?","tip":"Today everyone who remembers may be in the same room. Ask while the plates are mostly empty and nobody has stood up yet."},{"q":"Who hosted the big holiday meals when you were young, and what was their kitchen like?","follow":"What job were you given once you were old enough to help?","tip":"Leftovers day. Ask over a plate of them. It is the easiest setting there is."},{"q":"What dish showed up every year, made the same way every time? Who made it?","follow":"Where is that recipe now: on a card, in a book, or only in someone's head?","tip":"If the recipe lives only in their head, offer to cook it with them this month and write it down as you go."},{"q":"What holidays did the household you grew up in celebrate? Walk me through one of those days from the morning on.","follow":"What was the one rule everyone had to follow that day?","tip":"Do not assume you know the traditions. Ask, even if you think you know."},{"q":"What is the first winter you remember clearly? Where were you living?","follow":"How did you keep warm, and what did you wear outside?","tip":"Weather is an easy way into a memory. Cold rooms and snowed-in days come back fast."},{"q":"Tell me about a gift you gave someone that you are still pleased about.","follow":"How did you pay for it, or how did you make it?","tip":"Asking about a gift they gave, not one they got, takes them somewhere less expected."},{"q":"What is a gift you were given as a child that you remember, even a small one? Who gave it to you?","follow":"Where did you keep it?","tip":"Gifts were scarce in some homes. If that was true for them, ask what the day felt like instead."},{"q":"What did the house look like at the holidays when you were growing up? Who did the decorating, if anyone?","follow":"What happened to those things?","tip":"If anything survived, an ornament, a candle holder, a tablecloth, ask them to bring it out."},{"q":"Tell me about a holiday that went wrong. What happened?","follow":"Who still brings it up?","tip":"Disasters make the best holiday stories, and most of them are safe to laugh about now."},{"q":"Where did people gather around the holidays when you were young: a church, a temple, a hall, a neighbor's house? Describe walking in.","follow":"Who did you always see there?","tip":"If the answer is nowhere, ask where people gathered instead. For a lot of families it was the kitchen."},{"q":"What songs or music do you connect with this time of year? Where did you hear them?","follow":"Who sang along, and who refused to?","tip":"Play one of the songs tonight and see what it brings back."},{"q":"Tell me about a holiday you spent away from home. Where were you?","follow":"How did you mark the day there?","tip":"Holidays away are often the ones people remember best, because they were different."},{"q":"Tell me about the first holiday you hosted or planned yourself. Where was it?","follow":"What did you get wrong, and what did you get right?","tip":"Ask how it compared with the ones they grew up with. That comparison is a story in itself."},{"q":"Who was the person at every holiday who told the stories? What was one they always told?","follow":"How did they start it?","tip":"Ask for the story the way that person told it. A second-hand story is still worth keeping."},{"q":"What did you do on the long days off school in winter when you were a kid?","follow":"Who did you spend those days with?","tip":"Children's games and chores tell you a lot about a place and a time."},{"q":"What is a tradition from your family that faded out? When do you remember it happening last?","follow":"Why do you think it ended?","tip":"If it is one worth bringing back, this month is a good time to try it once together."},{"q":"What is a holiday you remember because it was different from all the rest? What made it different?","follow":"Who was missing that year, or who was there for the first time?","tip":"Different years stick and ordinary years blur. Start with the one that stands out."},{"q":"What did you look forward to most in December when you were young, and where did it happen?","follow":"Who made it happen?","tip":"Ask about the waiting. The anticipation is often remembered better than the day."},{"q":"What smell or taste means winter to you? Where does it take you?","follow":"Who was in that kitchen?","tip":"If you can make it this week, make it, and ask the question again while it is cooking."},{"q":"Tell me about the most crowded holiday you remember. Where did everyone sleep?","follow":"Who snored, who argued and who got up first?","tip":"Questions about logistics get people laughing. Sleeping arrangements are a classic."},{"q":"What is a letter or card you got around the holidays that you remember? Who was it from?","follow":"What did it say, as near as you can remember?","tip":"If there is a box of old cards somewhere, this is the week to open it together."},{"q":"What did your street or town look like at night this time of year when you were growing up?","follow":"Where did you walk, and who walked with you?","tip":"Ask what they could see from the window. Small details carry a whole place."},{"q":"Who is someone you used to spend the holidays with who is not here anymore? Tell me about one holiday with them.","follow":"What would they be doing right now if they were in the room?","tip":"This one can bring tears, and that is all right. Tears are not a reason to stop unless they say so."},{"q":"Tell me about a holiday in your twenties. Where were you living, and who were you with?","follow":"What did you think your life would look like by now?","tip":"Asking what they expected back then is a gentle way into how things turned out."},{"q":"What is the best New Year's Eve you remember? Where were you?","follow":"What were you hoping for that year?","tip":"Some people never cared for New Year's. If so, ask what they did instead."},{"q":"Tell me about a time someone outside the family was kind to you around the holidays. What happened?","follow":"What would you say to them now?","tip":"Kindness stories are good ones to share with the whole table."},{"q":"Who did you write to or call every year at this time? Tell me about them.","follow":"Where did they live, and what did you talk about?","tip":"A name from an old card list is a thread worth pulling."},{"q":"What did children do the night before a big holiday where you grew up? What did you do?","follow":"How did you try to stay awake, or how were you made to go to sleep?","tip":"If grandchildren are around, let one of them ask this one."},{"q":"Tell me about a holiday eve you remember clearly, whatever your family celebrated. Where were you?","follow":"What did you eat, and who was there?","tip":"If your family celebrates tonight, ask between courses. If not, a quiet evening is the best time of all."},{"q":"Which holiday tradition do you most want the family to keep? Tell me about the first time you remember it.","follow":"Who started it?","tip":"Write their answer down word for word and read it back at next year's table."}]},{"id":"veteran","name":"30 days with a veteran","calendarName":"A Question a Day: a veteran","kind":"evergreen","blurb":"Thirty questions for someone in your family who served, from the day they joined to what they want remembered. Starts the day after you add it.","note":"Let them lead. Skip anything they do not want to go into, and believe them the first time they say so.","credit":"Several topics follow the outline of the Library of Congress Veterans History Project sample interview questions (https://www.loc.gov/programs/veterans-history-project/how-to-participate/sample-interview-questions/). The wording is ours.","days":[{"q":"How did you come to join the service? Where were you living, and what were you doing when it was decided?","follow":"Who did you tell first, and how did they take it?","tip":"Let them lead. Skip anything they do not want to go into. This question starts before any of the hard parts, on purpose."},{"q":"Tell me about the day you left for training. How did you get there?","follow":"What did you bring with you?","tip":"Travel stories warm people up. Ask who was sitting next to them."},{"q":"What do you remember about your first few days of training? Pick one moment.","follow":"Who was the first person you got to know there?","tip":"Training is often where the funny stories live. Let them laugh."},{"q":"Who was in charge of you in training that you still remember? What did they look and sound like?","follow":"What is something they said that stayed with you?","tip":"Ask for the voice. People often remember exactly how an instructor said something."},{"q":"Once training was over, what did a normal day look like? Take me from waking up to lights out.","follow":"What was the food like?","tip":"Ordinary days are safer ground than big ones, and they are the part nobody else will remember."},{"q":"Who did you share quarters with? Tell me about one of them.","follow":"Where were they from, and what were they like?","tip":"Write every name down. Names are threads you can come back to."},{"q":"What did you keep with you, in a pocket or a bag, that you cared about?","follow":"Where is it now?","tip":"If they still have it, ask them to bring it out. Objects make it easier to talk."},{"q":"Tell me about a letter, call or package from home that you remember.","follow":"Who wrote to you most often?","tip":"If letters survive in a drawer, ask before reading any, and let them choose which ones."},{"q":"What is a place where you served that you can still picture? Describe it.","follow":"What was the weather like, and what did it smell like?","tip":"Let them pick the place. They may skip some, and that is their choice."},{"q":"Tell me about one day off that you remember. Where did you go?","follow":"Who were you with?","tip":"Days off are where the friendships show."},{"q":"What was your job day to day? Show me with your hands if it helps.","follow":"What part of it were you good at?","tip":"Asking what they were good at puts them in the expert's chair."},{"q":"Who do you still think about from your time in service? Tell me about them.","follow":"What would you say to them if they walked in?","tip":"This one can bring a long pause. Do not fill it. Count to ten in your head."},{"q":"What is the funniest thing you remember from your time in service?","follow":"Who was in on it?","tip":"Funny stories are a way in. More serious ones may come later, in their own time, or not at all."},{"q":"Tell me about a person you met in the service who was nothing like the people back home.","follow":"What did you learn from them?","tip":"People from somewhere else often explain a whole period of someone's life."},{"q":"Tell me about a holiday you spent in the service. Where were you?","follow":"What did people do to make it feel like a holiday?","tip":"Around any holiday, this is a gentle question for the table."},{"q":"What was the hardest part of being away? Answer as much or as little as you like.","follow":"What helped?","tip":"A good day to remind them they can skip anything. \"That's fine\" is all you need to say."},{"q":"What do people who were not there tend to get wrong about it? Where did you first notice?","follow":"What would you want them to understand instead?","tip":"People who will not talk about themselves will often happily correct a movie."},{"q":"Tell me about the day you found out you were going home, or getting out.","follow":"What did you do first?","tip":"Let them tell it in order. Do not jump ahead to how they felt."},{"q":"What was coming home like? Tell me about the first day or the first week.","follow":"Who did you see first?","tip":"Many veterans say nobody ever asked about this part. Take your time with it."},{"q":"What did you do for work after you got out, and how did you find that first job?","follow":"What from the service did you bring to it?","tip":"This connects the service years to the rest of their life. Ask about the bridge between them."},{"q":"Who from your service did you see again years later? Tell me about that day.","follow":"Who did you lose touch with that you still wonder about?","tip":"If a call or a letter still seems possible, write the name down."},{"q":"What did you keep from your service: papers, photographs, anything at all? Tell me the story behind one thing.","follow":"Who else has seen it?","tip":"Ask before handling anything. Let them hold it while they talk."},{"q":"Tell me about a conversation with your family about your service that you remember.","follow":"What did you want them to understand?","tip":"If you were part of that conversation, let them tell it their way first."},{"q":"What music brings that time back? Where were you when you heard it?","follow":"Who was with you?","tip":"If you can find the song, play it, then wait."},{"q":"What is a habit from the service you still have? When did you notice you still had it?","follow":"Who teases you about it?","tip":"Habits are a light way to talk about how the service stayed with them."},{"q":"Tell me about a Veterans Day or Memorial Day you remember from the years after. Where were you?","follow":"Who were you with?","tip":"Some veterans keep away from these days. If so, ask how they spend them instead."},{"q":"Tell me about a time someone younger asked you about your service. What did you tell them?","follow":"What did you save for another time?","tip":"If someone younger in the family is willing, let them ask today's questions."},{"q":"Think of your first day in the service. What would you tell yourself on that day?","follow":"Who gave you good advice back then?","tip":"Write down the advice in their exact words."},{"q":"What are you proudest of from that time? Tell me about the day it happened.","follow":"Who else knows this story?","tip":"Write it down in their words, not yours."},{"q":"What do you want the family to remember about your service? Tell me the story you would want told.","follow":"What would you rather we kept to ourselves?","tip":"Read back what you wrote and ask if you got it right. If they would like their story kept for good, the Library of Congress Veterans History Project collects interviews from families."}]}]};
